Recommends: homelab-database, homelab-pgbouncer, homelab-api
Description: OIDC-style SSO provider for the homelab-* ecosystem
 A Mojolicious app implementing an OAuth2/OIDC-style authorization-code
 flow (GET/POST /oauth/authorize, POST /oauth/token, GET /oauth/userinfo,
 GET /logout) so browser apps (homelab-drive, homelab-roundcube) can
 share one login: a live IdP session cookie here lets a second app's
 /oauth/authorize skip the login form entirely ("login once, login
 everywhere"), and /logout revokes the underlying homelab-api session
 centrally so every relying party's next introspect() call sees it die
 too ("logout once, logout everywhere") -- with no shared cross-app
 cookie and no id_token/JWKS to manage. Identity and credential
 verification are entirely delegated to homelab-api
 (Homelab::Common::AuthClient); this app owns only its own one-time
 authorization codes (`sso.oauth_codes`, split runtime/migrate roles,
 see CLAUDE.md).
